      ":question/id": "64b47bba-5a09-5496-b671-9f7f1f02b0e7",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n5{y}^{2}-y{e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y,\\,y\\ne 0.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-y{e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ -y{e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{y}^{2}-y & =0 \\\\ -y({e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y+1) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y+1 & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y+1) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y{e}^{x}+{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+{{(-5{e}^{x})}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{-{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5{e}^{x}y & =-{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-5{e}^{x}$ and $Q(x)=-{e}^{x}.$"
    },
